<% page title: "Customers",
        description: "The community organizations that run on Trellis, and how we work with them: as partners, not tickets." %>
<%
  kinds = [
    ["National networks and their chapters",
     "Networks with a chapter in every city use Trellis to give each chapter its own home while the network keeps one picture of the whole: who's active, what's been delivered, and where help is needed next."],
    ["Community events and gatherings",
     "Volunteer-run festivals and gatherings use it to publish their event pages, recruit and schedule volunteers, take artist and vendor applications, and check people in on the day."],
    ["Mutual aid and delivery programs",
     "Programs that collect and deliver supplies use it to track what partner agencies have asked for, plan deliveries against those requests, and record every drop-off."],
    ["Non-profits and b-corps",
     "Small teams use it as the place where members, volunteers, partners, surveys and reports finally live together."],
  ]

  practices = [
    ["We set it up with you",
     "Every new network gets a person, not a help-centre article. We sit down with you, learn how your work actually runs, and shape Trellis around it: your roles, your workflows, your fields, your words for things."],
    ["We build what's missing",
     "When your work needs something Trellis doesn't do yet, we build it with you as part of getting started: a new workflow, a report, a screen for the job your team does every week. You don't hire a consultant to customize a platform. That's what we're here for."],
    ["We bring your history in",
     "Most organizations arrive with years of spreadsheets. We help move them in, so the first day in Trellis already has your people and your past in it."],
    ["Your requests become the product",
     "Much of Trellis exists because a customer asked. The Budget and Reconciliation report mirrors the spreadsheet our networks already kept. Bulk recording, delivery goals and multilingual surveys all started as a conversation with the people who needed them."],
    ["We stay",
     "We keep talking after launch: check-ins through your busy season, a direct line when something goes wrong, and a seat at the table when we decide what to build next."],
  ]
%>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-12 pt-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20">
  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Our customers are our partners.</h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted sm:text-xl">
      Trellis is used by community organizations of every shape: national networks and their chapters,
      volunteer-run events, mutual aid programs, non-profits and b-corps. We don't think of them as accounts.
      We know their organizers by name, we've sat in their planning meetings, and a great deal of Trellis was
      built because one of them showed us what they needed.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="who-uses" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
  <h2 id="who-uses" class="section-title">Who runs on Trellis</h2>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    <% kinds.each do |title, body| %>
      <div class="card space-y-2">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-link-700"><%= title %></h3>
        <p class="text-ink-muted"><%= body %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="how-we-work" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
  <h2 id="how-we-work" class="section-title">How we work together</h2>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    <% practices.each do |title, body| %>
      <div class="card space-y-2">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink"><%= title %></h3>
        <p class="text-ink-muted"><%= body %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="privacy-note" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
  <div class="card space-y-3 p-8 sm:p-10">
    <h2 id="privacy-note" class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">Why you won't see logos here</h2>
    <p class="max-w-3xl text-ink-muted">
      The organizations we work with hold sensitive information about the people they serve, and many of them
      prefer to keep the tools behind their work quiet. We don't name a customer without their permission. If
      you'd like to talk to someone already running on Trellis, ask us and we'll introduce you to a network like yours.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-2 sm:flex-row">
      <a href="mailto:<%= Site::CONTACT_EMAIL %>?subject=Introduce%20me%20to%20a%20Trellis%20network" class="btn-warm-ghost">Ask for an introduction</a>
      <a href="<%= Site::SIGN_UP %>" class="btn-warm-primary">Start your network</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
